  "private": true,
  "//engines": "PINNED to one major, 24.x: the same as Vercel's project setting and every CI workflow's node-version (2026-11-09). It was >=22, which Vercel resolves to the NEWEST major, so production quietly ran Node 26 while CI tested 22, and it would have jumped again on the next release. Move all three together. @types/node stays at ^22: types BEHIND the runtime are safe (tsc only stops us using newer APIs); types AHEAD of it are not, as tsc would stop flagging APIs the deployed Node lacks.",
  "//yjs": "y-prosemirror, y-protocols and yjs are NOT used by our code — do not remove them as unused. BlockNote 0.54 moved them from its own dependencies to OPTIONAL peers, but @blocknote/core/dist/yjs.js still imports them at the top level and @blocknote/server-util imports that file unconditionally. src/lib/customDocs.ts loads server-util to render signing documents, so without these three declared the build fails with 'Module not found: y-prosemirror' and takes /signing/[token] with it. They were already in the tree before 0.54; the only change is that we now declare them instead of BlockNote. Drop them if BlockNote ever makes that import lazy.",
  "engines": {
    "node": "24.x"
  },
